                                                                  9228 1451
   Capture cross section                                          9228 1451
   Capture cross sections in EXFOR were measured mainly as        9228 1451
   ratios. At present we could not include them in the            9228 1451
   analysis. the Gwin data (EXFOR entry 14149003) are             9228 1451
   labelled as "derived" and do not have the uncertainties.       9228 1451
   Selected data for fitting were only:                           9228 1451
       M.Jandel,ET.AL.      (12)  X4 14149  3  2<E<60 keV         9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
  (n,2n)                                                          9228 1451
  The EXFOR entry #21568004 by J. Frehaut, which includes the     9228 1451
  normalisation correction for new Standards, was selected.       9228 1451
  Furthermore the data points below 8.5 MeV were rejected         9228 1451
  because of experimental uncertainties due to the difficulty     9228 1451
  in discriminating between neutrons from the (n,2n) and the      9228 1451
  fission reaction.                                               9228 1451
  The measurement #20795010 by D.S. Mather was rejected due       9228 1451
  to unreasonably large discrepancy with the Frehaut data         9228 1451
  and the shape, which was in contradiction with the model        9228 1451
  calculation.                                                    9228 1451
  Hence, selected data for fitting (n,2n) were only:              9228 1451
      J.Frehaut          (2016) X4 entry 21568004  E>8 MeV        9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
  (n,3n)                                                          9228 1451
  There are only two data sets in EXFOR. Only the data in the     9228 1451
  EXFOR entry 10795002 by Veeser were adopted, while the data     9228 1451
  in the EXFOR entry #20795011 by Mather were rejected.           9228 1451
  Hence, selected data for fitting (n,3n) were only:              9228 1451
      L.R.Veeser,ET.AL.    (78)  X4 10795  2                      9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Cross-material covariances were prepared manually from the      9228 1451
  Standards-2017 file. Unrecognised sources of uncertainties      9228 1451
  (USU) of 1.2 percent were added to the cross-covariances of     9228 1451
  the fission cross sections between different materials.         9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The uncertainties of the delayed neutron multiplicities were    9228 1451
  taken from Keepin rather than Tuttle, but taken from the        9228 1451
  publication by Tuttle, which includes a comparative analysis:   9228 1451
  R. J. Tuttle (1975) Delayed-Neutron Data for Reactor-Physics    9228 1451
  Analysis, Nuclear Science and Engineering, 56:1, 37-71,         9228 1451
  DOI: 10.13182/NSE75-A26620                                      9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The initial covariances for the prompt fission neutron          9228 1451
  multiplicities were taken from ENDF/B-VII.1, which originated   9228 1451
  from P. Young least-square fit of available nubar data.         9228 1451
  The following modifications were made:                          9228 1451
  * Below 0.7 eV an additional uncertainty component was added    9228 1451
    so as to make the uncertainty match the raw value             9228 1451
    recommended by Standards-2017.                                9228 1451
  * Between 0.7 eV and 73 eV the uncertainties were essentially   9228 1451
    taken from the experimental data, assuming they were          9228 1451
    statistical. In the range 5.6 eV to 75 eV an additional       9228 1451
    fully correlated component of 0.5 percent was assigned        9228 1451
    to account for the systematic uncertainty.                    9228 1451
  * Above 73 eV up to 20 keV no data experimental exist, hence    9228 1451
    a 2 percent uncertainty was assigned over energy subregions   9228 1451
    73, 100, 200, 400, 1000, 2000, 4000, 10000 and 20000 eV.      9228 1451
  * An additional 0.4 percent fully correlated uncertainty was    9228 1451
    added over the entire energy range from 1.E-5 eV to 30 MeV    9228 1451
    to account for the unrecognized systematic uncertaities of    9228 1451
    nubar measurements as recommended in Standards 2017.          9228 1451
  * Cross-material covariances are given for the nu-bar of        9228 1451
    U-233, Pu-239 and Pu-241 as evaluated with Standards-2017.    9228 1451
    The covariances are assumed energy-independent, although      9228 1451
    the values in Standards-2017 are applicable to the thermal    9228 1451
    energy region only.                                           9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The covariances of the Legendre elastic scattering component    9228 1451
  up to order P2 with cross-correlations as obtained in the       9228 1451
  prior are available in MF34.                                    9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The PFNS covariances were evaluated with the spectra. In the    9228 1451
  thermal range they correspond to Standards-2017. At higher      9228 1451
  energies the covariance evaluation was done at LANL together    9228 1451
  with the evaluation of the spectra.                             9228 1451
